        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Watchmaking - 02 The Verge Escapement",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The verge-and-foliot has no natural frequency. The foliot is a rigid bar with adjustable weights — it has **inertia** but no restoring force. Its oscillation period is not intrinsic; it depends on:"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-VERGE-ESCAPEMENT.md#026",
      "path": [
        "02-VERGE-ESCAPEMENT.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:watchmaking:02-verge-escapement, git-history:watchmaking:02-verge-escapement]",
        "canonical_path": "watchmaking/02-VERGE-ESCAPEMENT.md",
        "concepts": "[verge, escapement]",
        "current_path": "watchmaking/02-VERGE-ESCAPEMENT.md",
        "id": "maxim:watchmaking:verge-escapement",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "watchmaking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[verge, escapement]",
        "section": "watchmaking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Watchmaking - 02 The Verge Escapement",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "1. **Driving torque:** More force from the falling weight = faster oscillation. As the weight falls and the rope winds onto different drum diameters, torque varies.\n2. **Friction:** Changes with temperature, lubricant condition, wear.\n3. **Foliot mass distribution:** The weights can be moved inward/outward to adjust the rate, but this is a rate *setter*, not a natural frequency *keeper*.\n4. **Impulse geometry:** The angle and shape of the pallet-tooth interaction affect how hard the crown wheel pushes the pallets — and thus how fast the foliot swings."
    },
